# Migration plan task 4: was `Hecks.hecksagon "Inbox"` -- a stale
# leftover from before this file's own bluebook (inbox.bluebook)
# domain-renamed "Inbox" -> "IssueLog" to resolve a basename collision
# with aggregates/framework/inbox/bluebook/inbox.bluebook's OWN,
# unrelated real "Inbox" domain. Never updated to match. verify! looks
# up `bluebook(hexagon.domain)` using the HECKSAGON's own declared name,
# not the bind's own "IssueLog::Inbox" text -- so this file's bind was
# silently being checked against framework's REAL Inbox aggregate
# instead of IssueLog's, and once the earlier hecksagon-merge fix (this
# same migration pass) made multi-file hecksagons for the same domain
# actually accumulate instead of silently overwriting, the two binds
# collided visibly ("Inbox::Inbox has 2 authoritative persisted_by
# bindings").
Hecks.hecksagon "IssueLog" do
  IssueLog::Inbox.persisted_by("Heki")
end
